\f0\fs48\b\cf1 TextEdit 1.20, unmodified\b0\cf0\par
\fs24 Bundle \b com.apple.TextEdit\b0, version \b 1.20\b0, build \b 415\b0. The executable is \f1 782,384\f0 bytes. Its SHA-256 is checked before the launch and again after the screenshot. A mismatch stops the run.\par
\fs32\b\cf2 What the shim adds\b0\cf0\par
\fs24\pard\li360
\bullet  \b Frame.\b0  \i CGRect.frame(withWidth:using:)\i0 reorders registers into \f1 NSFrameRectWithWidthUsingOperation\f0.\par
\bullet  \b Documents.\b0  \f1 readFromURL:\f0 goes through \f1 NSRichTextReader\f0, which already parses RTF.\par
\bullet  \b TextKit 1.\b0  The TextKit 2 defaults are forced off, so TextEdit builds an \f1 NSLayoutManager\f0.\par
\pard\li0\fs32\b\cf3 Checked, and not changed\b0\cf0\par
